** Small-scale yielding, In718 bicrystal with single-crystal plasticity (UMAT), written by make_gpe_model.py from slice_3D.inp
** bicrystal: grain 1: In718 (anisotropic), Bunge (105.0, 60.0, 30.0); grain 2: In718 (anisotropic), Bunge (0.0, 0.0, 0.0)
** K_I=1264.911, K_II=0.000, K_III=0.000 [MPa*sqrt(mm)], a=20.0 mm, crack tip=(0.0, 0.0) mm, alpha=0.0 deg
** In718_bicrystal_ssy_bc.inp: u1, u2, u3 of the analytical field on all nodes of the boundary node columns
** In718_bicrystal_ssy_equations.inp: *EQUATION u_i(z) = u_i(z_min) for all other node columns
**
*Heading
Generalised plane-strain K-field model: grain 1: In718 (anisotropic), Bunge (105.0, 60.0, 30.0); grain 2: In718 (anisotropic), Bunge (0.0, 0.0, 0.0)
**
** Slice of thickness t = 0.01 mm of the 2D boundary-layer model (same in-plane mesh, mid-side nodes at the
** crack front at the quarter point, t = 0.25), one
** element layer, node levels z = 0, t/2, t: 6912 C3D20 elements, 59376 nodes. Units: mm, N, MPa.
** Crack tip on the z-axis, crack along the negative x-axis (seam), outer radius R = 10 mm (inner mesh up to r = 1 mm unchanged, outer ring added by make_larger_model.py).
**
** Section, material (crystal orientation), boundary condition and the generalised plane-strain
** constraints are defined by make_gpe_model.py (the section/material of slice_3D.inp are
** placeholders), see README.md in this folder.
**
** Sets: BULK        all elements
**       BOUNDARY    all nodes of the outer boundary (r = R) on the levels z = 0, t/2, t
**       BOUNDARY_GRAIN1, BOUNDARY_GRAIN2   the same nodes split into grain 1 (y > 0) and grain 2
**                   (y < 0, incl. the lower crack face), for the app with the interface model
**       CRACK_FRONT_*, CRACK_TIP_*   crack-tip node on z = 0 (BOTTOM), t/2 (MID), t (TOP)
**
*Preprint, echo=NO, model=NO, history=NO, contact=NO
